---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { components, elementCount } from '../data/site.ts';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const pkgs = [
  ['@bixboards/design-system', 'Design tokens and theming: JSON themes compiled to CSS custom properties.'],
  ['@bixboards/core', `${components.filter((c) => c.pkg === 'core').length} general-purpose components, the virtualizer and utilities.`],
  ['@bixboards/data-table', 'Virtualized enterprise data table (bx-data-table).'],
  ['@bixboards/data-list', 'Virtualized list/grid and tree (bx-data-list, bx-virtual-tree).'],
  ['@bixboards/react · angular · svelte', 'Generated wrappers over the custom elements.'],
] as const;
---

<Base title="Getting started · Bixboards" description="Install Bixboards, register components, theme them and use them in React, Angular or Svelte.">
  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="page-title">Getting started</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Bixboards is {elementCount} custom elements across a few packages. Install what you need,
        import the components you use, and style them with tokens.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Install</h2>
      <pre class="code"><code>pnpm add @bixboards/core @bixboards/design-system
# optional data modules
pnpm add @bixboards/data-table @bixboards/data-list</code></pre>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {pkgs.map(([name, purpose]) => <tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{purpose}</td></tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>2. Add the tokens</h2>
      <p>
        Components read colors, spacing and type from CSS custom properties. Generate them from a theme
        with the design-system CLI and load the stylesheet once. Set <code>data-theme</code> on the
        root element to pick a theme; this site switches between <code>board</code> and
        <code>board-dark</code>.
      </p>
      <pre class="code"><code>{`pnpm exec bixboards-ds build --theme themes/board.json --theme themes/board-dark.json --out src/styles/generated

/* app.css */
@import './generated/tokens.css';

<html data-theme="board">`}</code></pre>

      <h2>3. Use a component</h2>
      <p>Importing a component's path registers its tag. Everything is tree-shakeable, so only what you import ships.</p>
      <pre class="code"><code>{`<script type="module">
  import '@bixboards/core/button';
  import '@bixboards/core/input';
</script>

<bx-input label="Email" type="email"></bx-input>
<bx-button>Subscribe</bx-button>`}</code></pre>

      <h3>Custom tag names</h3>
      <p>
        Import <code>/define</code> instead to register under your own tag, which avoids collisions
        and lets two versions coexist. Nothing is registered until you call the function.
      </p>
      <pre class="code"><code>{`import { defineButton } from '@bixboards/core/button/define';

defineButton('acme-button');`}</code></pre>

      <h3>Properties and events</h3>
      <p>
        Primitive options are attributes. Objects and arrays (<code>columns</code>, <code>data</code>,
        <code>items</code>) are properties. Custom events are prefixed <code>bx-</code>, bubble and are
        composed.
      </p>
      <pre class="code"><code>{`const table = document.querySelector('bx-data-table');
table.columns = [{ field: 'name', header: 'Name', sortable: true }];
table.data = rows;
document.addEventListener('bx-remove', (event) => console.log(event.target));`}</code></pre>

      <h2>4. Frameworks</h2>
      <p>Generated wrappers add typed props and events and import the element for you.</p>
      <pre class="code"><code>{`// React
import { BxButton } from '@bixboards/react/bx-button';
<BxButton variant="secondary" onClick={save}>Save</BxButton>

// Angular (standalone components)
import { BxButton } from '@bixboards/angular/bx-button';

// Svelte
import BxButton from '@bixboards/svelte/BxButton.svelte';`}</code></pre>

      <h2>5. Scale and theme</h2>
      <p>
        One token, <code>--bx-scale</code>, rescales spacing, type and radii. Put it on any element
        that also has <code>class="bx-scale"</code> to scale a region, such as a dense data grid,
        independently. Components reflow with container queries, so they adapt to the space they are
        given rather than the viewport.
      </p>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="bx-scale" style="--bx-scale: 0.8; display:flex; gap:.5rem; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap">
          <bx-button size="s">Compact</bx-button>
          <bx-input label="Search" placeholder="Scaled to 0.8" style="max-inline-size:14rem"></bx-input>
          <bx-badge>0.8×</bx-badge>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="code"><code>{`<div class="bx-scale" style="--bx-scale: 0.8">
  <bx-button size="s">Compact</bx-button>
</div>`}</code></pre>
      <p>
        Every component also exposes CSS custom properties and parts for styling; they are listed in
        the API section of each <a href={`${base}/components/`}>component page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
